 "notes": "North is up. The plate's neat line is at about x 5440 (key and title beyond it). Liberty is 50' except between Western Av. and Freeman, where it widens to ~80' on its north side; Western/Liberty and Freeman/Liberty are taken at the mean of the two centrelines (y~912), Faulkner/Liberty and points further west on the 50' centreline (y~930-936). Faulkner (30') ends at an unnamed ~18 ft E-W alley (y~3488) that runs east from Denman and dead-ends at x~4800. Sedgewick St. does not reach President Place: its bed east of a diagonal line (x~2243 on the centreline) is filled by a 1-2 story frame building (recorded as an end). Hoefer (20'; spelled HOEFER, 1904 Hoeffer) runs Flint to Kenner. President Place (60', no bracketed name) runs Kenner to Hopkins along Lincoln Park and is ~150 px west of Hoefer at Kenner. East of Freeman only the mouths of adjoining-sheet streets are drawn (Armory Av., Clinton St., Wise Alley, Betts St., Laurel St., Stevenson Al., Hopkins); the unnamed alleys at y~4010 (between Armory and Clinton; Clayers Alley on 1904 sheet 71) and y~5582 (between Betts and Laurel) are in alleys. STEVENSON AL. is the 1904 Stephenson Alley. Harriet St. (~33 ft) and Louisa St. (~21 ft) run south from Hopkins off the bottom of the plate. Wade jogs ~28 px north east of Freeman (4-corner centre used). Hopkins is 80' west of Freeman and ~40' east of it, and 60' west of Dalton / 80' east of it (4-corner centres). Freeman's centre bows from x~5058 (Liberty) to ~5079 (Kenner) and back to ~5067 (Hopkins) in the scan. Water pipes are drawn as solid lines inside the streets and were not used as street lines. No bracketed old names seen on this half. Gutter overlap with 22-9L: Curran/Kenner, Curran/Hopkins and the eight Dalton intersections (Liberty to Hopkins)."
